%I A401250 #11 Nov 05 2026 19:33:09
%S A401250 6,12,18,20,24,28,30,36,40,42,48,54,56,60,66,72,78,80,84,88,90,96,100,
%T A401250 102,104,108,112,114,120,126,132,138,140,144,150,156,160,162,168,174,
%U A401250 176,180,186,192,196,198,200,204,208,210,216,220,222,224,228,234,240,246,252,258,260,264
%N A401250 Numbers k such that the minimum number of odd terms in a 2-dense sublist of divisors of k is greater than 1.
%C A401250 Indices of A401249 where the terms are greater than 1.
%C A401250 First differs from A005835 (pseudoperfect numbers) at n=83.
%H A401250 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A401250/b401250.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A401250 350 is the 83rd pseudoperfect number which has three 2-dense sublists of divisors: [1, 2], [5, 7, 10, 14, 25, 35, 50, 70], [175, 350]. The minimum number of odd terms in a 2-dense sublist is 1, so 350 is not in the sequence.
%e A401250 352 has only one 2-dense sublist of divisors: [1, 2, 4, 8, 11, 16, 22, 32, 44, 88, 176, 352]. The sublist contains two odd numbers (1 and 11) hence the minimum number of odd terms in the 2-dense sublist is 2, so 352 is in the sequence.
%t A401250 A401250Q[k_] := Min[Map[Count[#, _?OddQ] &, Split[Divisors[k], #2 <= 2*# &]]] > 1;
%t A401250 Select[Range[2, 300, 2],A401250Q] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 30 2026 *)
%Y A401250 Cf. A005835, A018406, A018408, A174973 (2-dense numbers), A237271, A384222, A384225, A401249.
